          {"id":"amz_ds_e2","year":"Amazon SDE-1 OA 2023","q":"Minimum number of queues needed to implement a stack?","opts":["1","2","3","4"],"ans":0,"exp":"You can implement stack with 1 queue by rotating elements. Push: enqueue new element, then rotate all others behind it. Pop: simply dequeue from front."},
          {"id":"amz_ds_e3","year":"Amazon Intern OA 2024","q":"Height of a complete binary tree with n nodes?","opts":["n","n/2","log₂(n)","n²"],"ans":2,"exp":"Complete binary tree height = ⌊log₂(n)⌋. At each level, the number of nodes doubles. Level 0=1, level 1=2, level k=2^k nodes."}
