          {"id":"amz_ds_h2","year":"Amazon SDE-1 2024","q":"LRU Cache: Which data structures implement it in O(1) get/put?","opts":["Array + BST","HashMap + Doubly Linked List","Queue + Set","Stack + HashMap"],"ans":1,"exp":"HashMap gives O(1) lookup. Doubly Linked List maintains order (most→least recent). HashMap stores (key → DLL node) pointers. On access: move node to head. On eviction: remove tail. LeetCode #146."}
