          {"id":"amz_oop_e3","year":"Amazon Intern 2023","q":"Difference between abstract class and interface in Java?","opts":["No difference","Abstract class can have method implementations; interface cannot (pre-Java 8)","Interface supports multiple inheritance; abstract class does not","Both are correct"],"ans":3,"exp":"Both B and C are correct. Abstract class: can have concrete methods + state (fields). Interface: only abstract methods (pre-Java 8), supports multiple inheritance to avoid diamond problem."}
